You are a senior Flutter engineer. We are building "Souqi" (سوقي), an offline point-of-sale and invoice app for small grocery shops in Syria. Read this whole brief, then wait for the phase prompts I send next. Do not write code yet — reply only with: (1) the folder structure you will use, (2) the packages you will use with one-line reasons, (3) the full SQLite schema, (4) any questions or risks.

PLATFORM & STACK
- Android only (phones and tablets). Flutter stable, Dart 3, null-safety, Material 3.
- 100% offline. No server, no internet, no accounts, no analytics. All data in a local SQLite database (sqflite).
- State management: flutter_riverpod. Keep a clean layered structure: data (db, repositories) / domain (models) / features (screens, providers).
- Android package id: com.souqi.app (I may change it later).

LANGUAGES
- Full Arabic and English UI using flutter_localizations + ARB files (app_ar.arb, app_en.arb). No hard-coded user-facing strings anywhere.
- Arabic is RTL, English is LTR. Layout must mirror correctly.
- App language and INVOICE language are two separate settings (e.g. Arabic UI, English invoice). Default: Arabic for both.
- Use a font with good Arabic support (e.g. Cairo or Tajawal via bundled asset, not network).

CORE FEATURES (later phases)
1. Products: name, optional short code (e.g. "101"), unit, price, favorite flag, active flag. Fast search by name or code.
2. Units: preset list (kg, g, bag, piece, box, liter) + user-defined units. Quantities can be decimals (0.5 kg).
3. Sale screen: add items by tapping favorites, searching, or typing a code; set quantity; live total; save + print invoice.
4. Invoice settings (fully dynamic, stored in DB): paper width (80 mm default, 58 mm, or custom mm), printer DPI (203 default), side margins, base font size, shop name, logo, header text, footer text, invoice language, and toggles for which fields to show (item code, unit, unit price, date/time, invoice number).
5. Printing to a Bluetooth ESC/POS thermal printer. Arabic text must print correctly, so the invoice is rendered as a Flutter widget, captured to an image at the exact printable width in dots, converted to monochrome and sent as an ESC/POS raster image. Also share the invoice as PDF (WhatsApp etc.).
6. Invoice archive: search by date range / invoice number / product, view, reprint, delete one, delete a date range, and auto-delete invoices older than N days (user setting, off by default).
7. Statistics: sales total, invoice count, average invoice, top products by quantity and by amount, for today / this week / this month / custom range, plus comparison with the previous period.
8. Extras: bulk price change by percentage (all or selected products, with rounding option), barcode scan with camera, discount per invoice (amount or %), favorites bar, data backup/restore to a single file, PIN lock for settings/archive/stats.
9. Debt ledger (customer debts) — BUILD IT but HIDE IT behind a compile-time feature flag.
10. Multiple currencies (fully offline, rates entered manually by the shop owner):
   - Currencies table: code, Arabic name, English name, symbol, decimal places, exchange rate to the base currency, active flag, sort order. Seed SYP (base, 0 decimals) and USD (2 decimals); the user can add any currency (e.g. TRY, EUR, or "old lira" for the Syrian redenomination) and edit/disable them.
   - One BASE currency (default SYP) used for totals and statistics. The user can change the base currency only with a clear warning and a recalculation step.
   - Each product has its own price currency (e.g. sugar priced in SYP, a carton of oil priced in USD). On the sale screen every line is converted to the invoice currency using the current rate.
   - Per sale the user can choose the invoice currency (default = base). The invoice can optionally show the total in up to 2 extra currencies (e.g. "Total: 400 SYP ≈ 0.04 USD"), configurable in invoice settings.
   - Quick "update exchange rate" action reachable from the sale screen in two taps, showing when the rate was last updated.
   - Every invoice stores a SNAPSHOT of the currency, the rate(s) used and each line's original price + original currency, so changing rates never changes old invoices.

FEATURE FLAGS
- lib/config/features.dart with `const bool debtEnabled = false; const bool barcodeEnabled = true; const bool discountEnabled = true;`
- When a flag is false, nothing related to it appears anywhere (menus, buttons, invoice lines, stats). The DB tables still exist from version 1 so enabling later needs no migration.

DATA RULES (important)
- Money: store as INTEGER minor units of its currency (SYP with 0 decimals = whole pounds, USD with 2 decimals = cents), always together with its currency code. Quantities: store as INTEGER thousandths (500 = 0.5) to avoid floating-point errors. Line total = round(price * qty / 1000).
- Exchange rates: never use double for stored rates. Store each rate as an INTEGER scaled by 1,000,000 (rate_micro), meaning "1 unit of this currency = rate base units". Do conversions with integer/BigInt math and one explicit rounding step (half-up) at the end, to the target currency's decimal places. Put all money/currency math in one tested module.
- Invoice items store a SNAPSHOT of product name, code, unit and unit price at sale time, so later price changes never alter old invoices.
- Invoice numbers are sequential from a persisted counter and never reuse numbers, even after deletion.
- Use versioned migrations (onCreate + onUpgrade with explicit version steps). Never drop user data in a migration.
- Wrap multi-step writes (saving an invoice + its items) in transactions.

